Run order: build once -> Habitat -> robot model -> RViz -> runner (map) -> motion planner (path).
Wait for each step's "ready" line before starting the next one.

terminal 1  (build once - do NOT rebuild while the other terminals are running)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
rm -rf build install log
colcon build --packages-select robo_project vinebot_description
source install/setup.bash

terminal 2  (Habitat)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
python3 src/robo_project/habitat_bridge_vinebot_2.py
# ready when: "Robot spawned at x=-4.10 y=4.90" and "Habitat Bridge fully initialized"
# options:  --ros-args -p start_x:=-4.1 -p start_y:=4.9 -p start_yaw:=0.0
#           -p gpu_device_id:=-1    (no NVIDIA GPU / VM: software rendering)
#           -p show_window:=false   (no camera window)

terminal 3  (robot model)

cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch vinebot_description robot_launch.py

terminal 4  (RViz: map, robot, planned path, goal, current waypoint)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
rviz2 -d src/vinebot_description/config/display_vinebot.rviz

terminal 5  (runner: publishes /map + follows /planned_path)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 run robo_project runner_node
# ready when: "MAP BROADCAST SUCCESSFUL! Check RViz now."  -> map appears in RViz

terminal 6  (motion planner: A* from the robot to the goal)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 run robo_project motion_planner
# plans to GOAL_X/GOAL_Y (0,0) at start; the robot drives it in Habitat and RViz.
# Click "2D Goal Pose" in RViz to send a new goal - it re-plans from the current pose.
# If the robot gets stuck on something that is not on the sketch, runner_node
# reports it on /blocked_point and motion_planner re-plans around it.






=====================================================================
CMN MODE: ML local occupancy + localization on the sketch (no ground-truth pose)
=====================================================================
The planner/runner are the same, but their /odom is remapped to /cmn/odom:
the robot first finds itself on the hand-drawn map, then plans and drives.
Extra Python deps in the habitat env:  pip install torch opencv-python

terminal 1  (build once)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
colcon build --packages-select robo_project vinebot_description
source install/setup.bash

terminal 2  (Habitat - any spawn point, the robot is NOT told where it is)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
python3 src/robo_project/habitat_bridge_vinebot_2.py --ros-args -p start_x:=3.5 -p start_y:=4.5

terminal 3  (robot model)           ros2 launch vinebot_description robot_launch.py
terminal 4  (RViz)                  rviz2 -d src/vinebot_description/config/display_vinebot.rviz
    add displays:  Map /cmn/belief (color scheme "costmap"),  Map /cmn/local_occ,
                   PoseWithCovariance /cmn/pose

terminal 5  (runner + ML + localization + planner, all remapped)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch robo_project cmn.launch.py
# add  log_gt_error:=true  to also print the error vs the Habitat pose (evaluation only)
# the robot explores until "LOCALIZED after N updates", then motion_planner plans
# from the estimated pose to the goal and runner_node drives it.

Re-train the local occupancy model (optional)

conda activate habitat
python src/robo_project/cmn_nav/generate_dataset.py --scene src/environment/IMR_lab8.glb --samples 10000 --out data/imr_lab8.npz
python src/robo_project/cmn_nav/generate_dataset.py --scene src/environment/Denmark.glb --samples 4000 --out data/denmark.npz
python src/robo_project/cmn_nav/train.py --data data/imr_lab8.npz data/denmark.npz --out src/robo_project/ml_runs/cmn_local_occ.pth
